1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,351
So I'll start with some tips specifically for visiting grasmere since if you are short on time this is where I would suggest you visit.
先说几个专门针对格拉斯米尔的经验；如果时间有限，作者会建议去这里。

2
00:00:07,361 --> 00:00:12,231
Our first and last hike started from here so it really does have everything.
我们的第一次和最后一次徒步都从这里出发，所以它确实很齐全。

3
00:00:12,241 --> 00:00:17,281
To park the car specifically for hiking I'd suggest the lancrigg hotel.
如果是为了徒步而停车，作者当时推荐的是 Lancrigg 酒店。

4
00:00:17,281 --> 00:00:25,510
The cost of parking can be redeemed for food and drink at the hotel and it was a great rest spot after the hike.
停车费可以抵酒店里的餐饮消费；而且徒步结束后，这也是个很好的歇脚处。

5
00:00:25,520 --> 00:00:33,281
Now we walked past the gingerbread shop four times and it always had a long queue apart from its last hour of trading.
我们四次经过姜饼店，除了营业结束前的最后一个小时，每次都排着长队。

6
00:00:33,281 --> 00:00:38,391
It was tasty enough though that it still would have been worth the wait but do bear the queues in mind.
不过姜饼确实很好吃，就算要等也值得；但还是要把排队这件事考虑进去。

7
00:00:38,401 --> 00:00:47,510
There was also a side entrance that people didn't seem to be aware of that sold most of the same products as inside so do check if that's open too.
还有一个侧门，似乎不少人不知道；那里卖的东西大多和店里一样，所以作者也提醒看看那个门是否开放。

8
00:00:47,520 --> 00:00:52,080
The hotel we stayed at was literally in the middle of everything we visited in this video.
我们住的酒店，真就位于这段视频里所有游览地点的中间。

9
00:00:52,080 --> 00:01:00,881
Grasmere ambleside and bowness were all a 15 minute drive away with keswick and aira force being 30 and 40 minutes away.
格拉斯米尔、安布尔赛德和鲍内斯都在十五分钟车程内；凯西克和艾拉瀑布则分别约三十和四十分钟。

10
00:01:00,881 --> 00:01:08,481
The included breakfast was clearly very good lake windermere just a minute away along with its ferry that can take you further south.
包含在房费里的早餐显然很好；温德米尔湖仅一分钟之遥，那里还有能带你继续向南的渡船。

11
00:01:08,481 --> 00:01:13,591
For our dates the room and breakfast was 120 pounds per night.
按我们出行时的日期，房间加早餐每晚是一百二十英镑。

12
00:01:13,601 --> 00:01:20,711
I'll leave a link in the description below to check prices for your dates along with other options in the area.
我会把链接放在下方说明栏，供你查看自己出行日期的价格，也会附上当地其他选择。

13
00:01:20,721 --> 00:01:26,961
On the subject of paying for stuff since covid England is becoming more and more a cashless society.
说到付款，作者觉得，自疫情以来，英格兰正在越来越多地转向无现金社会。

14
00:01:26,961 --> 00:01:35,910
Which personally speaking for me is great but for international tourists just something to keep in mind as several places wouldn't take any cash at all.
就我个人而言这很好，但国际游客得记着这一点，因为有些地方完全不收现金。

15
00:01:35,920 --> 00:01:41,521
Amongst others the pub we visited in keswick was card only the gingerbread shop was card only.
比如我们在凯西克去的酒馆只收卡，姜饼店也只收卡。

16
00:01:41,521 --> 00:01:47,591
And even the 40 p entrance fee for the public toilets were all contactless.
甚至公共厕所四十便士的入场费，也都是用非接触式支付的。

17
00:01:47,601 --> 00:01:50,231
But don't melt your gold down just yet.
不过，先别急着把你的金子都熔了。

18
00:01:50,241 --> 00:01:57,030
On the flip side some parking machines are still coins only so it's worth having a stack of change in the morning.
反过来说，有些停车收费机仍然只收硬币，所以早上带些零钱还是值得的。

19
00:01:57,040 --> 00:02:03,191
Most machines did have options but the one we parked at for derwent water was coins only.
大多数机器的付款方式不止一种，但我们在德文特湖停车处用的那台只收硬币。

20
00:02:03,201 --> 00:02:10,641
It's also definitely worth downloading both the pay by phone parking and ring go app before arrival.
作者也觉得，抵达前下载 Pay by Phone Parking 和 Ring Go 这两个应用很有用。

21
00:02:10,641 --> 00:02:16,081
Between them both they covered most car parks and allows you to top up your meter remotely.
两者合起来，覆盖了大多数停车场，还可以远程给停车计时续费。

22
00:02:16,081 --> 00:02:21,121
I say download them before since the countryside isn't known for its fast internet speeds.
我之所以说要提前下载，是因为乡间可不以网速快出名。

23
00:02:21,121 --> 00:02:27,111
And downloading a 100 megabyte app is not fun on 0 5 g.
用作者戏称的“零点五 G”网络下载一个一百兆的应用，可不是什么愉快体验。

24
00:02:27,121 --> 00:02:35,040
Overall on the subject of driving I actually found the roads to be a lot easier to drive than say the cotswold trip that we had last year.
总体说到开车，我其实觉得这里的路，比我们去年去科茨沃尔德那次好开得多。

25
00:02:35,040 --> 00:02:40,800
There weren't as many tiny countryside roads and all destinations were connected by dual carriageway.
这里狭窄的乡间小路没那么多，各个目的地之间都有分隔式双向道路相连。

26
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:49,920
As a direct comparison to the cotswolds as a holiday I think the landscapes are definitely more epic in the lake district but the cotswolds feels more uniquely english.
直接比较这两个度假目的地，我觉得湖区的景观更壮阔，科茨沃尔德则更有独特的英格兰味道。

27
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:54,841
If that makes any sense so it depends on what is more important to you as a countryside getaway.
不知道这样说是否说得通；所以，就看你在乡间度假时更看重什么。

28
00:02:56,001 --> 00:03:00,641
Also for the countryside I was actually very surprised by how many buses there were.
另外，作为乡间地区，这里的公交车数量之多，确实让我很惊讶。

29
00:03:00,641 --> 00:03:06,561
It clearly wasn't london frequency but they seemed good enough that you could do most of what we did without a car.
班次显然没有伦敦那么密，不过看起来已经足以让你不自驾，也能完成我们大部分的行程。

30
00:03:06,561 --> 00:03:15,351
It would lose a lot of the convenience obviously but I'd be interested to hear in the comments below how people have found using buses around this region.
当然，便利性会损失不少；不过我很想在评论区听听，大家实际在这一带坐公交的体验如何。
